From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CADCraft <noreply@cadcraft.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:33:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(compile): build from a clean checkout without the web
 runtime payload

slab-compile embedded gen/web-runtime/slab-runtime.js and
clients/web/wasm/slab_kernel_bg.wasm with include_str!/include_bytes!. Both
are untracked products of `just web-runtime`, so `cargo build -p slab-compile`
failed on a fresh clone, and so did every use of the crate as a Cargo git
dependency.

- New feature `wc-embed` (default on). The build script embeds the two files
  when the feature is on and both exist (cfg `slab_wc_payload`); when either
  is missing it warns and the crate still builds. With the artifacts present
  nothing changes: `just gen`, `just check`, `just test` and the packaging
  flow embed exactly what they did.
- `wc::HAS_PAYLOAD` says which build this is. Without the payload
  `wc::generate` and `react::generate` return the module, declarations and
  SLIR without the two sidecars, and `slab gen wc` / `slab gen react` refuse
  with a sentence naming `just web-runtime` instead of writing an empty
  runtime.
- The version hash: the build script takes `SLAB_GIT_HASH` from the
  environment when set, and otherwise only trusts `git rev-parse` when the
  enclosing checkout's root is this workspace. A copy of the crate nested in
  another repository used to report that repository's HEAD; it now reports
  `unknown`.
